      "servedBy": "meta-models/muse-spark-open-1026",
      "text": "Single-base drawer limit is enforced by the configurator's placement rules, not a mesh error. A `full` hex base (`piece:0,0,0;full`) offers **zero** drawer sockets (`find_sockets family:drawer` → 0 offers). A cut-face half base (`half-n`/`half-s` etc.) offers **one** drawer socket (`key:s` on the cut face) - verified by placing `half-n` and getting `s14`/`s15` and successfully adding `drawer:0#0,0#cut`. Multi-storey drawer sockets also return 0. No combination of drawer sockets on a solitary cell reaches five, and adding the neighbour cells needed for `notch`/`bay` bins/drawers would violate \"nothing else added beside or on top.\"\n\nBuild left as a single full base to honour the \"single hex base, nothing else beside or on top\" rule exactly.\n\n",
